-- title:
--   Ends of the blown-up supersingular chart: cyclic decomposition and crossings
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ are primes with $\ell\neq q$, $M'\ge 1$ is an integer with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, $L$ is a field of characteristic $0$, and $\xi\in L$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity for which there exists a ring homomorphism $\iota_0:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota_0\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$ (hypothesis `hι`). The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(t)\!)$ pinned by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(t)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   The base is a discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with $L$ as its fraction field and with a scalar tower $A\to L\to K$; further $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`). The element $j\in K$, nonzero, has Laurent series the coefficientwise image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion $t^{-1}\cdot(\text{jNum})$ of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Finally $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $j$-finite chart algebra, i.e. the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element `jChartFin` $=j$; `XFin` $=\operatorname{Spec} C$; and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the scheme obtained as the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and the $j^{-1}$-finite chart along the middle chart, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and the canonical morphism `ιFin` from `XFin` into it. The ideal $y\subset C$ is maximal (`hy`), contains $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a Drinfeld chart at every supersingular point, seven clauses, summarised here) asserts: for every point $z$ of the two-chart model, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ equal to the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ and satisfying the same supersingularity condition as `hss`, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S=W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(\,C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\,)$, such that, writing `toC` for the completion map, `mkS` for the quotient map and `germY` for the canonical map $C\to$ stalk at $z$: (i) $e$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau\in\operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ` preserves $C$; (iii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ such $\tau$ act trivially modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such $\tau$ acting trivially modulo $y'$ there are $\theta\in\operatorname{Aut}(S)$ transporting $\tau$ through $e\circ{}$`toC`$\circ{}$`germY`, a scalar $c\in W$ and a matrix $M$ over $W$ with $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; (v) primes of $S$ lying over $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$ and carrying tangent directions $(a_1:b_1)$, $(a_2:b_2)$ with $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ have distinct contractions to the stalk; (vi) for a prime of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$ with tangent direction $(1:0)$, an element $a\in C$ has germ in its contraction precisely when every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) the Hasse germ clause: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-expansion over $L$ with all exponents multiplied by $q\ell$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for a suitable $a_0\in A$ with difference in $y'$ there are $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose leading $e_0$-form $\sum_{i}\operatorname{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, and $e(\mathrm{germ}(j\text{-element}-a_0))=$ class of $h$.
--
--   A particular point and chart are then fixed: $z$, $\varpi_z$ with `hϖz`, `hz`, a point $y'$ of `XFin` over $z$ with `hy'`, the supersingularity `hss'` of $y'$, and `hy'y` : $y'=y$ as ideals of $C$; together with data $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1$ (units `hu₁`, `hv₁`, congruence `hf₁`, $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ by `hσ₁`) and an isomorphism $e_1$ onto $S_1=W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this witness the same seven clauses (i)–(vii) as above.
--
--   The ideal $J\subset C$ is pinned by `hJ` to be the infimum, over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau$ satisfying the level-automorphism condition at $\gamma^{-1}$ and preserving $C$, of the pullback along $\tau|_C$ of the contraction, along $e_1\circ{}$`toC`$\circ{}$`germY`, of the ideal generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. The $A$-subalgebra $B\subseteq K$ is pinned by `hB` to be the subalgebra generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$. Finally $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and the following four hypothesis groups are imposed. `hR1`: $C\subseteq B$, and every $f\in K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq0$. `hR2`: $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): the elements of $L$ lying in $W$ are exactly those of $A$; $\mathfrak m_W=(\varpi)$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ iff $b\in\mathfrak m_W$; and $f\in W$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses): first, for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $=k[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1)$ whose kernel is the set of $b\in B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, which is compatible with $A\to k$, and which is equivariant: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ there is $c\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) — the kernel of $(g,c)\mapsto\det(g)c^{q+1}$ on $GL_2(\mathbb Z/q)\times\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ — such that $\rho\circ\tau$ is `hAction` of that element composed with $\rho$, and $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; secondly, such $\tau$ preserve $B$; thirdly, every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit: some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ carry every $b\in B\cap\mathfrak m_W$ into that prime; fourthly, if $b\in B$ has all such translates in $\mathfrak m_W$ then $\varpi\mid b$ in $B$; fifthly, a level automorphism attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist: an integer $n\ge1$ dividing $q+1$; an element $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; an automorphism $\tau_0\in\operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ satisfying the level-automorphism condition at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ and preserving $W$; an integer $m\ge1$ with $\varpi^m=\varpi_t\cdot(\text{unit})$; an element $\zeta_0$ of $\hat A=$ `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A` with $\zeta_0^n=1$ and $\zeta_0^k-1$ a unit for $0<k<n$; the membership of [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) in $K$ and in $C$, together with $a_0\in A$ such that this element minus $a_0$ lies in $y$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K$, such that the following hold.
--
--   (1) $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B$ pointwise. (2) For each $0<k<n$ some element of $B$ is moved by $\tau_0^k$. (3) Every $\tau$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and preserves $W$ agrees on $B$ with $\tau_0^k$ for some $k<n$. (4) `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements. (5) For $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, each $O\in$ `ends` satisfies $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$ for some $O'\in$ `ends`. (6) For any $O,O'\in$ `ends` there are $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ with $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$. (7) Each $O\in$ `ends` is stable under $\tau_0$. (8) Distinct $O,O'\in$ `ends` are separated: some $f$ lies in both and is a non-unit of $O$ but a unit of $O'$. (9) There is an $A$-subalgebra $B_c\subseteq K$ of finite type over $A$, stable under every level automorphism attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, with $B_c\subseteq O$ for every $O\in$ `ends` and $O$ the localisation of $B_c$ at the elements of $B_c$ that are units of $O$ (that is, $f\in O$ iff $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in B_c$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$). (10) For $O\in$ `ends`, $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, if $\tau(O)\subseteq W$ then $\tau$ preserves $W$.
--
--   (11) Each $O\in$ `ends` satisfies $O\subseteq W$ and is a local Noetherian ring for which: $C\subseteq O$; the elements of $L$ lying in $O$ are exactly those of $A$; and every $f\in O$ is congruent to some element of $A$ modulo the non-units of $O$ (there is $a\in A$, with $a\in O$, such that $f-a$ is not a unit of $O$). Moreover $\varpi\in O$ and there exist $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` $\hat A\,\hat\varpi^{\,m}=\hat A[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(X_0X_1-\hat\varpi^{\,m})$, units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, an $\hat A$-algebra automorphism $\theta_0$ of it, an inverse $\zeta_0'$ of $\zeta_0$, and a local ring structure on the model, such that: $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $a$ in $\hat A$; $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak m_W$ and $c_x$ does not; the Hasse germ lies along $V$, namely `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`$-a_0$ belongs to $O$ and $\iota$ sends it to $w_V\cdot V^{e}$ for some unit $w_V$ and some $e\ge1$; $\iota$ transports $\tau_0$ to $\theta_0$ (for $f\in O$ with $\tau_0 f\in O$); and $\theta_0(U)\equiv\mathrm{const}(\zeta_0)\,U$, $\theta_0(V)\equiv\mathrm{const}(\zeta_0')\,V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal of the model. In addition there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K$ with: $O\subseteq W_x$; $C\subseteq W_x$; the elements of $L$ in $W_x$ exactly those of $A$; $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring with $\mathfrak m_{W_x}=(\varpi)$; an element $t\in W_x$ such that for every $p\in A[X]$, if $p(t)\in\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ then all coefficients of $p$ lie in $\mathfrak m_A$; the same property for `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)` in place of $t$; $c_x\in\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ and $c_y\notin\mathfrak m_{W_x}$; for $b\in C$, $b\in\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ implies $b\in y$, while some $b\in y$ lies outside $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$; every $O'\in$ `ends` other than $O$ contains an element not in $W_x$; and if $O'\in$ `ends` and some level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ sends $O'$ into $W_x$, then $O'=O$. Finally there is an $A$-subalgebra $B_x\subseteq K$ with: $B_x\subseteq B\cap O$; $B_x$ of finite type over $A$; $B_x$ stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; every $f\in B_x$ has $\operatorname{ord}_P f\ge0$ at every place $P$ of $K$ over $L$ (a valuation subring of $K$ containing $L$, proper, with principal ideals) at which $\operatorname{ord}_P j\ge0$; $O$ equal to the localisation of $B_x$ at its elements that are units of $O$; and an element $b\in B_x$ which detects $O$: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ is $A$, with $\varpi\in\mathfrak m_V$, and such that $j\in V$ with no monic polynomial in $j$ over $A$ taking a value in $\mathfrak m_V$, if some element of $O$ fails to lie in $V$ then $b\notin V$.
--
--   (12) Valuative cover: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ is $A$, which contains $C$ and which carries $y$ into $\mathfrak m_V$, either $B\subseteq V$, or there is $O\in$ `ends` with $O\subseteq V$ and with every non-unit of $O$ lying in $\mathfrak m_V$.
--
--   This is the local structure theorem at a supersingular point of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ over a henselian discrete valuation base: after passing to the weighted blow-up algebra $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$, it produces the $q+1$ branches ("ends") of the exceptional Drinfeld fibre with their crossing presentations over $\hat A[\![U,V]\!]/(UV-\varpi^m)$, the cyclic group of order dividing $q+1$ acting on $B$, the Igusa valuation subrings separating the branches, and a valuative covering criterion. It is used by the assembly of the supersingular affine chart with its ends, Hasse germ and inertia data, which feeds the comparison of $X_H$ with the Drinfeld curve at $q$.
